our title:Evolution of social media platforms (MySpace to
Facebook/Instagram/TikTok)

First viewpoint analysis:
With the evolution of social media came with impacts on how companies run their businesses and how society functions around the usage of social media.
For businesses, social media brought new ways to advertise and sell products for customers to buy. On the societal aspect, it was able to allow
people new ways to communicate with each other, as well as making it easier to talk to other people from around the globe. Right now, we are going to be looking at
the business aspect of the evolution of social media, to see how companies were able to adapt to the ever-changing land scape of social media business.

A way that major brands were able to bring more attention to their business was through advertisements on social media platforms. Advertisements on social
media was introduced as early as 2006 with Facebook, after that was Twitter enabling ads in 2010, then other sites such as Snapchat, YouTube and more adding
ads to their platforms. Companies saw this as an opportunity to make their brands more popular, so they started to use social media as a way to grow. So, they started
putting ads on these sites either in picture or video form to inform people about their products or recruit them for their company. Even making the some of the ads
entertaining to some degree to entice people. Other social media sites even created accounts on their competitors' websites to advertise and talk about upcoming
updates to their own platforms.

According to Yoesoep Edhie Rachmad on his book 'Like, Share, Sell: Social Media for the Aspiring Business Owner,' he explains how the rise of social media has
given businesses the ability to look at real time data of their costumers to get a good idea of topics such as "engagement rates, follower demographics, and
content reach" to truly understand their audience and use that data to help improve aspects of their company to bring more success to the business as
a whole. Despite these features being able to massively help business owners, including some on the smaller side of the spectrum, he does warn to not put too
much reliance on quantitative metrics. These sets of data do not capture the heart and soul of human connection. Which he argues that the success of social media
mainly comes from the ability to listen, respond, and adapt in ways that corresponds to the ever-changing interests or demands of their audience.

With social media rapidly being used more as an essential tool for companies to grow their businesses, this brought along an increased need for said businesses to
implement an all-in-one solution for their growing social media presence. So, a way that companies chose to deal with this is by implementing Sprinklr, which is an 
an AI native SaaS enterprise software company that can allow brands to manage everything about their social media strategy in "one complete system". With this
all-in-one system, comes with advanced and customizable governance workflows, asset management, monitoring, audience profiling, campaign execution, and analytics.
These solutions can help any brand achieve their strategic goals without much push back or hassle thanks to Sprinklr. These tools can help assist marketers as
well, with their goal towards an Omi-channel ecosystem. Which is when a business's social media is directly connected to website, email content, online
reputation management, and even offline channels. This social data will allow brands to more accurately research and show their new products, while also being
able to predict a crisis in customer sentiment.
